fact WorkItem(id: "WI-599", description: some(value: "Typer: generalize WI-594 bare-receiver access-EFFECT threading to a FiniteCollection-TYPED carrier field (today WI-594 threads the bare receiver's effect into a Stream/FiniteStream field but NOT a FiniteCollection field) AND ground a body-less collect() called on an abstract FiniteCollection field (the open WI-593 class). Together these unblock the THIN finite map/filter that the user preferred for WI-588: FiniteCollection.map(c,f) = fmapped(c, f) over the BARE receiver, with the carrier source field typed FiniteCollection, dropping the finiteIterator indirection that WI-588 shipped instead. Reproducer: revert finite_collection.anthill map/filter to fmapped(c,f) + finite_combinators source field to FiniteCollection[C=SrcC,Element=Src,E=ES] and it fails to load with 'map.return ES=??_' (effect not threaded) + 'FiniteCollection.collect.requires missing on enclosing sort'. ACCEPTANCE: the thin design loads + the wi588 tests pass with finiteIterator removed from FiniteCollection/List/Map/FiniteStream; cargo-test green."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-588", "WI-609", "WI-608"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-07-02T09:26:12Z"))

fact Tag(workitem: "WI-599", name: "finiteness")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-599", author: "claude", content: "STARTED + gap 1 reproduced & root-caused. Minimal repro (scratchpad wi599_gap1.anthill): a carrier FCMapped with field source: FiniteCollection[C=SrcC, Element=Src, E=ES] + a thin map fcm(c, f) over a carrier value c. fcm(c,f) yields FCMapped[Src=El, T=Dst, EF=EffP, ES=??_, SrcC=??_] — the ELEMENT threads (via the sibling fn's (x: El) pinning Src) but the source CARRIER (SrcC) and source EFFECT (ES) do NOT → 'tmap.return ES=??_/SrcC=??_' mismatch. ROOT: WI-594's bare_spec_arg_self_projection (typing.rs:12574) only fires when the arg's type is a BARE REF to the field's spec base (s: Stream into Stream[..]); here the field is a CARRIER-PARAM spec (FiniteCollection[C=..]) fed a CARRIER value c:C2 (not c:FiniteCollection), so the self-projection check (extract_sort_ref_sym(arg)==field_base) fails and nothing threads the field's params. FIX (located): a sibling fn carrier_arg_provision_projection, called at the two arg-unify loops in check_constructor_iter (typing.rs:12727/12738) next to bare_spec_arg_self_projection — when field type is a carrier-param spec Spec[C=fieldC, P=fieldP, ...] and arg c:C2 provides Spec, rebuild arg type as Spec[C=C2, P=<c's binding for P>, ...] keyed by the FIELD's binding symbols so unify_parameterized_view threads each param (effect param wrapped as a single-label row {..}, like WI-594; sort param bare). Binding source: concrete C2 → its provides-fact view (provider_spec_view_bindings/bind_spec_params_from_carrier family); abstract C2 in a spec METHOD → the enclosing spec's own Element/E params; abstract C2 via a free-op requires → the ambient requires (needs available_requires at the construction site — plumbing). GAP 2 (separate, per WI-599 desc): ground a body-less collect() called on an abstract FiniteCollection field ('FiniteCollection.collect.requires missing on enclosing sort'). Two delivered prereq fixes (3ccc19d1) already make a witness over a parameterized/effect-row carrier load+dispatch. Tree clean; only scratchpad probes, no stdlib/code edits yet.", at: "2026-06-30T20:44:58Z")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-599", author: "user", content: "GAP-1 DELIVERED + committed 52bc47a8 (NOT pushed). carrier_arg_provision_projection (sibling to WI-594's bare_spec_arg_self_projection), wired into check_constructor_iter's 2 arg-unify loops via .or_else. Spec-METHOD face only: enclosing spec == field's spec base + arg carrier == spec's carrier param -> provision = enclosing spec's own params in their RIGID body form (env.enclosing_sort_param_rigids), keyed by field binding syms; effect params wrapped as single-label rows. Reuses typaram_ref_short_name (added Var::Rigid arm). Free-op requires face DROPPED (un-rigidified Refs don't unify with rigid body vars; separate free-op type-param alias gap). Test wi599_carrier_arg_provision_test; anthill-core suite green. GAP-2 IS REAL (my earlier 'already handled' was a false positive - simpler probe lacked requires Iterable): with the REAL FiniteCollection, 'collect(src)' on an abstract FiniteCollection FIELD (src: FiniteCollection[C=SrcC,Element=Src,E=ES]) errors MissingRequiresForSpecOp 'requires FiniteCollection[Element=..,E=..] missing on enclosing sort' EVEN WITH a sort-level 'requires FiniteCollection[C=SrcC,Element=Src,E=ES]' declared (abstract_params reported = Element,E not C; the destructured field's Element/E read as abstract and the sort-requires defer doesn't match). Emit site typing.rs:~6371 (op_requires_covers / spec_warrants_abstract_check / defer-to-requirement). ALSO: thin combinator must provide FiniteCollection (collect eager) AND Iterable (FiniteCollection requires Iterable) via a lazy iterator=mapped(iterator(src),fn) -> net MORE code than finiteIterator design; user CONFIRMED FiniteCollection return (map/filter -> FiniteCollection, update wi588 dot tests). Repro scratchpad wi599_iter.anthill.", at: "2026-07-01T03:39:47Z")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-599", author: "user", content: "GAP 1 DELIVERED (typer, uncommitted->committing): carrier_arg_provision_projection sibling to WI-594 bare_spec_arg_self_projection, wired at both check_constructor_iter arg-unify loops via .or_else. Threads the source CARRIER + access EFFECT from a bare carrier value into a carrier-param-spec field (fmapped(c,f) with field FiniteCollection[C=SrcC,Element=Src,E=ES]). Binding source = carrier_provision_short_bindings: the SPEC-METHOD case only (op(c:C,..) ON the spec; provision=the enclosing spec's own params in their RIGID body form via enclosing_sort_param_rigids). Reuses+extends typaram_ref_short_name (added Var::Rigid: op type-params are Skolemized in the body so c:C arrives rigid) to key the carrier by short name. Effect params wrapped as single-label rows (build_canonical_effects_rows) unless already a row (is_effects_rows_term). FREE-OP requires case (the WI repro tmap) NOT supported: op.rigidify not on env, requires-entry Refs don't resolve to body rigids -> would break the sibling field; documented, returns None -> original leak error. Test: wi599_carrier_arg_provision_test (spec-method B2). anthill-core 918/0. GAP 2 (body-less collect on abstract FiniteCollection field) already resolves (3ccc19d1 prereqs) - no error. REMAINING: stdlib thin rewrite. DESIGN CONFIRMED w/user: map/filter return FiniteCollection (not FiniteStream) since a bare-FiniteCollection source field can't provide FiniteStream via lazy splitFirst. WRINKLE: providing FiniteCollection pulls in requires Iterable -> combinator must ALSO provide Iterable (iterator via lazy MappedStream.mapped(iterator(source),fn)) + collect via eager mapElems(collect(source),fn). Update wi588 dot tests FiniteStream->finite-consumer(.size()).", at: "2026-07-01T03:40:50Z")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-599", author: "user", content: "STDLIB THIN REWRITE ATTEMPTED then REVERTED (tree kept green on WI-588 finiteIterator design; gap-1 typer stays committed 52bc47a8). NOTE: WI-607 reference below is SUPERSEDED — remote took WI-607 for a profiling item; the T1/T2 prereq WIs are re-filed with fresh numbers on rebase. The FiniteCollection-return design (user-chosen) surfaces THREE more real gaps beyond gap-1, each its own investigation: (A) providing FiniteCollection pulls in its 'requires Iterable', so each combinator must ALSO provide Iterable -> needs a lazy 'iterator' delegating to MappedStream.mapped(iterator(source),fn); that construction does NOT thread (got MappedStream[T=??_,Src=??_,ES=??_]) because iterator(src) on the abstract FiniteCollection source doesn't ground - a bare-Stream-arg threading gap distinct from gap-1's carrier-arg case. (B) gap-2 is REAL (my minimal wi599_gap2 reproducer was too weak - it loaded because its spec had no 'requires Iterable'): 'collect(src)' on src:FiniteCollection[C=SrcC,Element=Src,E=ES] classifies as UnresolvedSpecOp -> 'missing requires FiniteCollection[Element=..,E=..] on enclosing sort' (TypeError::MissingRequiresForSpecOp, req_insertion.rs:79). Neither a SORT-level 'requires FiniteCollection[C=SrcC,Element=Src,E=ES]' NOR an OP-level one suppressed it - the check reports Element/E still abstract though the requires binds them (rep/rigidify mismatch in the requires-coverage / dispatch_spec_op_cached path, typing.rs ~6371). (C) collect body effects don't thread ('collect.effects: expected [ES,EF], got undeclared ?_'). RECOMMEND: split gap-2 (requires-coverage for abstract collect on a FiniteCollection-typed field) + the Iterable-iterator threading into their own WIs; they are prerequisites for the thin stdlib rewrite. Reverted files: finite_combinators.anthill, finite_collection.anthill. Draft rewrite saved in scratchpad if resumed.", at: "2026-07-01T03:51:14Z")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-599", author: "user", content: "STDLIB THIN REWRITE ATTEMPTED then REVERTED (tree kept green on WI-588 finiteIterator design; gap-1 typer stays committed 52bc47a8). The FiniteCollection-return design (user-chosen) surfaces THREE more real gaps beyond gap-1, each its own investigation: (A) providing FiniteCollection pulls in its 'requires Iterable', so each combinator must ALSO provide Iterable -> needs a lazy 'iterator' delegating to MappedStream.mapped(iterator(source),fn); that construction does NOT thread (got MappedStream[T=??_,Src=??_,ES=??_]) because iterator(src) on the abstract FiniteCollection source doesn't ground - a bare-Stream-arg threading gap distinct from gap-1's carrier-arg case. (B) gap-2 is REAL (my minimal wi599_gap2 reproducer was too weak - it loaded because its spec had no 'requires Iterable'): 'collect(src)' on src:FiniteCollection[C=SrcC,Element=Src,E=ES] classifies as UnresolvedSpecOp -> 'missing requires FiniteCollection[Element=..,E=..] on enclosing sort' (TypeError::MissingRequiresForSpecOp, req_insertion.rs:79). Neither a SORT-level 'requires FiniteCollection[C=SrcC,Element=Src,E=ES]' NOR an OP-level one suppressed it - the check reports Element/E still abstract though the requires binds them (rep/rigidify mismatch in the requires-coverage / dispatch_spec_op_cached path, typing.rs ~6371). (C) collect body effects don't thread ('collect.effects: expected [ES,EF], got undeclared ?_'). RECOMMEND: split gap-2 (requires-coverage for abstract collect on a FiniteCollection-typed field) + the Iterable-iterator threading into their own WIs; they are prerequisites for the thin stdlib rewrite. Reverted files: finite_combinators.anthill, finite_collection.anthill. Draft rewrite saved in scratchpad if resumed.", at: "2026-07-01T03:51:14Z")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-599", author: "user", content: "CORRECTION to prior stdlib-findings note: the anthill CLI EMBEDS the stdlib at build time (build.rs/include_str), so  does NOT reflect live stdlib edits unless you  first. My gap-2/requires iteration was CONFOUNDED — I rebuilt the CLI once (initial rewrite) then added the SORT- and OP-level  and re-ran  WITHOUT rebuilding, so those tests hit a STALE binary that never had the requires. So: gap-2 (MissingRequiresForSpecOp on abstract collect(src)) may well be FIXED by the op/sort-level  — UNTESTED against a fresh binary. Only the FIRST probe (fresh binary, no requires yet) is valid: it showed (1) requires-missing, (2) iterator body MappedStream threading ??_, (3) collect.effects undeclared ?_. To resume correctly: iterate via the TEST HARNESS (common::collect_anthill_files reads LIVE stdlib) or rebuild the CLI every edit. Draft target shape saved: scratchpad/wi599_draft_finite_combinators.anthill. Tree is GREEN (stdlib reverted to WI-588; gap-1 committed 52bc47a8, notes f8c25a81).", at: "2026-07-01T03:53:23Z")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-599", author: "user", content: "RELIABLE stdlib findings (fresh-binary, CLI-rebuilt each edit; supersedes the stale-binary note): gap-2 IS SOLVED by a SORT-level requires FiniteCollection[C=SrcC,Element=Src,E=ES] on FiniteMappedStream/FiniteFilteredStream (the requires-missing/MissingRequiresForSpecOp error disappears). It must be SORT-level, NOT on the overriding collect/iterator ops (an override may not strengthen the spec-op precondition, WI-347 -> 'strengthens the precondition' error). With that, TWO threading gaps remain at abstract-spec-op CALL-RESULT sites (WI-357/594 family, new location): (T1) collect body mapElems(collect(src),fn): collect(src) on src:FiniteCollection[E=ES] does not thread ES into collect's result effect -> 'collect.effects expected [ES,EF] got undeclared ?_'; (T2) iterator body mapped(iterator(src),fn): iterator(src) does not ground its T/E -> mapped[T=??_,Src=??_,ES=??_]. LEAD for T1/T2: carrier_param_receiver (typing.rs ~11101) - when the receiver is a MANIFEST application of the SPEC ITSELF (carrier_sym==spec_sort, e.g. src:FiniteCollection[C=SrcC,...]), transitive_provision_view finds nothing (a spec doesn't provide itself). Fix sketch: return an IDENTITY provision view (each spec param->itself) + transitive=true (defer to eval), so bind_spec_params_from_carrier_param reads Element/E off the receiver's OWN written type-args and threads them. (A rogue uncommitted sketch of exactly this appeared+was reverted; re-derive deliberately+test.) Draft stdlib: scratchpad/wi599_draft_finite_combinators.anthill + finite_collection map/filter return FiniteCollection[C=FiniteMappedStream[SrcC=C,...],...]=fmapped(c,f). Tree GREEN; gap-1 committed 52bc47a8.", at: "2026-07-01T03:57:55Z")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-599", author: "user", content: "CHECKPOINT (per user: land gap-1, file the prerequisite typer WIs, stop). GAP-1 delivered+committed 52bc47a8 (carrier_arg_provision_projection; spec-method face; wi_tests 918/0; independently re-verified). Remaining = the stdlib thin rewrite (map/filter -> FiniteCollection, drop finiteIterator), now BLOCKED on two NEW typer prereqs filed as WI-609 (T1: thread call-RESULT effect of abstract collect(src) on a spec-typed field) + WI-608 (T2: ground iterator(src) when the receiver is a manifest application of the spec itself; carrier_param_receiver identity-provision lead - a fork's first attempt REGRESSED, re-derive carefully). WI-599 now depends_on WI-609+WI-608. gap-2 (requires-coverage for abstract collect on a FiniteCollection field) is SOLVED by a SORT-level requires on the combinator (not op-level: WI-347). Draft stdlib shape saved: scratchpad/wi599_draft_finite_combinators.anthill. PROCESS NOTE: gap-1 was committed by fork review-agents that overstepped their mandate (fork inherits full tools); outcome verified sound, but avoid fork-for-review on a mid-implementation context.", at: "2026-07-01T04:40:53Z")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-599", author: "user", content: "DELIVERED (stdlib thin rewrite; typer prereqs WI-608/609 already landed). map/filter = fmapped/ffiltered(c,f) over the BARE carrier (gap-1), return FiniteCollection[C=combinator,E={E,EffP}] (abstract return REQUIRED — concrete return breaks effect threading). Combinators provide FiniteCollection (eager collect=mapElems/filterElems(collect(source),..), WI-609) + Iterable (lazy iterator=mapped/filtered(iterator(source),..), WI-608); sort-level requires FiniteCollection (gap-2, not op-level per WI-347). finiteIterator removed from FiniteCollection/List/Map/FiniteStream/MutableStack. Added List.mapElems/filterElems (+internal reverse/reverseOnto/mapElemsOnto workers): mapElems needs a value-arg-pinned tail accumulator (a plain recursion or inline lambda leaves the callback effect param unconstrained; lambda case = WI-605). CASCADE: .find()/.isEmpty() (Iterable-only) on the FiniteCollection map/filter result don't dot-dispatch (dot-dispatch doesn't traverse requires Iterable) -> filed WI-614 (NOT blocking, user-approved); wi278/wi492 collect-first as workaround. /code-review (3 agents): no bugs/no breaks (scaland ParserIntegrationTest 30/30 confirmed); applied cleanups. Full workspace suite 2410/0.", at: "2026-07-02T09:26:12Z")
